<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0-windows</TargetFramework>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);MSTEST0032;MSTEST0037;CS0067</NoWarn>
    <!--
      Deliberately absent from VeloxDev.slnx: the solution is the only thing `dotnet test` at the repository root
      resolves, so not being in it is what keeps the root command backend-only. Run this project by path.
    -->
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MSTest" Version="4.0.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="coverlet.collector" Version="6.0.4">
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <!--
      The UI drivers reach the demos through UI Automation. FlaUI has not been maintained since 2022, so it is kept
      behind Drivers/AutomationLocator.cs: every FlaUI type in this project lives there, and swapping to the
      framework's own System.Windows.Automation is a one-file change.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="FlaUI.Core" Version="4.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="FlaUI.UIA3" Version="4.0.0" />
    <!--
      The Blazor driver drives its demo through a browser rather than a desktop window, which is what makes that
      platform runnable on an agent. Only the base package is referenced, not Microsoft.Playwright.MSTest: that one
      pins its own MSTest and would fight the 4.0.2 metapackage above. The browser and its context are managed by
      Engine/BlazorHost.cs instead, and it launches against the installed Edge (Channel "msedge"), so nothing has to be
      downloaded to run the suite locally. A CI image without Edge runs playwright.ps1 install chromium once and drops
      the channel.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Playwright" Version="1.62.0" />
    <!--
      FlaUI.Core 4.0.0 pins System.Drawing.Common 5.0.2, which carries GHSA-rxg9-xrhp-64gj and would otherwise fail
      the build on NU1904. A direct reference wins over the transitive one and pulls the patched assembly in; FlaUI
      only uses it for screenshot capture, so nothing it does depends on the old behaviour.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="System.Drawing.Common" Version="10.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Using Include="Microsoft.VisualStudio.TestTools.UnitTesting" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
